    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "jyvnxll",
      "content": "Plant pathology is the scientific study of plant diseases caused by pathogens (infectious agents) and environmental conditions (abiotic factors). It encompasses the mechanisms of disease development, diagnosis, and management strategies."
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "Plant pathology studies plant diseases, their etiology, disease cycles, and management strategies.",
      "id": "g0i90o9"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3j0moye",
      "content": "Disease Triangle: For a disease to occur, three factors must coincide: Susceptible Host + Virulent Pathogen + Favourable Environment. This is the fundamental concept of plant disease epidemiology."
    },
