      "content": "4.4 Principles of Plant Disease Management"
    },
    {
      "id": "g4redxo",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Principle</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Methods</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Examples</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Exclusion</p>",
            "<p>Prevent pathogen entry into a region</p>",
            "<p>Quarantine, seed certification, import regulation (PQ Act)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Eradication</p>",
            "<p>Eliminate established pathogen</p>",
            "<p>Roguing, burning infected crop debris, soil fumigation</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Protection</p>",
            "<p>Prevent infection of healthy plants</p>",
            "<p>Fungicide sprays, seed treatment, physical barriers</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Immunisation (Resistance)</p>",
            "<p>Use of resistant varieties</p>",
            "<p>Breeding for disease resistance; IARI, ICRISAT varieties</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Biological Control</p>",
            "<p>Use natural enemies of pathogens</p>",
            "<p>Trichoderma viride, T. harzianum; Pseudomonas fluorescens; Bacillus subtilis</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Chemical Control</p>",
            "<p>Fungicides, bactericides, nematicides</p>",
            "<p>Systemic (Carbendazim, Propiconazole); Contact (Mancozeb, Copper)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Cultural Control</p>",
            "<p>Modify environment unfavourable for pathogen</p>",
            "<p>Crop rotation, deep summer ploughing, intercropping, proper spacing</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Integrated Disease Management</p>",
            "<p>Combination of all methods</p>",
            "<p>IPM approach; reduces chemical use; sustainable</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
